}
```

New:
```js
function createLi(t) {
    var li = document.createElement('li');
    li.setAttribute('data-id', t.id);

    var view = document.createElement('div');
    view.className = 'view';

    var toggle = document.createElement('input');
    toggle.className = 'toggle';
    toggle.type = 'checkbox';
    toggle.addEventListener('change', function () { onToggle(t.id); });

    var label = document.createElement('label');
    label.addEventListener('dblclick', function () { startEdit(t.id); });

    var destroy = document.createElement('button');
    destroy.className = 'destroy';
    destroy.addEventListener('click', function () { onDestroy(t.id); });

    view.appendChild(toggle);
    view.appendChild(label);
    view.appendChild(destroy);

    var edit = document.createElement('input');
    edit.className = 'edit';
    edit.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { onEditKey(t.id, e); });
    edit.addEventListener('blur', function () { onEditBlur(t.id); });

    li.appendChild(view);
    li.appendChild(edit);
    updateLi(li, t);
    return li;
}

function updateLi(li, t) {
    if (t.completed) {
        li.classList.add('completed');
    } else {
        li.classList.remove('completed');
    }
    var toggle = li.querySelector('.toggle');
    if (toggle) {
        toggle.checked = t.completed;
    }
    if (!li.classList.contains('editing')) {
        var label = li.querySelector('label');
        if (label) {
            label.textContent = t.title;
        }
        var edit = li.querySelector('.edit');
        if (edit) {
            edit.value = t.title;
        }
    }
}

function render() {
    var vis = visibleTodos();
    var visById = {};
    vis.forEach(function (t) { visById[t.id] = t; });

    // Remove rows whose todo no longer belongs in the visible list.
    var existing = Array.prototype.slice.call(todoListEl.children);
    existing.forEach(function (li) {
        if (!visById[li.getAttribute('data-id')]) {
            todoListEl.removeChild(li);
        }
    });

    // Update existing rows in place, or create new ones, in visible order.
    var placed = {};
    vis.forEach(function (t, idx) {
        var li = todoListEl.querySelector('[data-id="' + t.id + '"]');
        if (!li) {
            li = createLi(t);
        } else {
            updateLi(li, t);
        }
        var current = todoListEl.children[idx];
        if (current !== li) {
            todoListEl.insertBefore(li, current || null);
        }
    });

    var activeCount = ...
    ... rest unchanged ...
}
```

Wait, there's a subtlety with `querySelector('[data-id="' + t.id + '"]')`. The id contains characters like `-` and alphanumerics; the selector `[data-id="..."]` with the value quoted is fine. But ids could contain characters that break the attribute selector? uid() produces `Date.now().toString(36) + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2,8)` — only alphanumerics and `-`. Safe in a quoted attribute selector. Good. (The existing startEdit/onEditBlur already use this same `querySelector('[data-id="' + id + '"]')` pattern, so it's consistent.)

Now `updateLi` is called in createLi after building, to set initial state. Good.

One concern: when creating a new li, I call updateLi which sets label.textContent and edit.value and toggle.checked and completed class. Good.

Edge: the `placed` variable I declared but don't use. Remove it.

Edge: ordering. After removing non-visible, the remaining children are the visible ones (subset). Then for each visible todo in order, I find its li (existing or create) and insertBefore at idx. This correctly orders. Good.

Edge: when a todo is toggled complete in 'active' filter, it's removed from visible. Its li is removed. Good — matches existing behaviour (hides it).

Edge: editing mode preservation across render. If a render happens while a row is editing (e.g. toggle another todo while editing one), updateLi skips clobbering label/edit for the editing row. The 'editing' class persists on the li (we never remove it in render). Good. The current code would've lost editing state entirely (rebuild). So in-place is strictly better.

